  (label "TX_SW_A"
    (at 71.12 77.47 0)
    (fields_autoplaced yes)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "c59fe443-2653-407d-be9c-27c1e3c78c37")
  )
  (text "AIRCRAFT AUDIO I/O - rebuilt 2026-10-20, per Peter. Relays K1 (TX select)\nand K2 (RX mute) removed. History of the relay design: git log on this\nfile (commits 6e258c8 .. e763f7c).\n\nJ5 = aircraft TRS (PJ068 adapter): Tip = mic out to aircraft (MIC_TIP),\nRing = earphone audio in (RX_RING), Sleeve = aircraft ground (AC_GND).\n\nTX - MIC TO AIRCRAFT, U12 (Panasonic AQW612S, 1 Form A + 1 Form B)\n- N.C. (7-8): BOOM_MIC (J4.1) <-> MIC_TIP. Closed with no LED current, so\n  with power or control lost the pilot's boom mic reaches the aircraft.\n- N.O. (5-6): TX_INJ <-> MIC_TIP. AeroNode speaks only while driven.\n- The aircraft's 8-16 V mic bias still flows DC-direct Tip -> U12 N.C. ->\n  J4 capsule -> AC_GND; nothing in that loop blocks DC. U12 is rated 60 V\n  (48 V recommended), 1-2.5 ohm on, vs the mic's 220-2200 ohm source.\n- Drive: RLY_COIL_SUPPLY (U11, 4.5 V) -> R15 220R -> LED 1-2 -> LED 3-4\n  (pins 2-3 linked) -> TX_SW_K -> Q1 (2N7002, low side) <- GPIO_RLY_TX_SEL_3V3,\n  R10 100k gate pulldown. ~10 mA typ, >=6 mA worst case (Panasonic\n  recommends 5-30 mA). GPIO low or high-Z = boom mic.\n- Unchanged from the relay design: T1 SM-LP-5001 600:600 isolates only\n  the AeroNode leg (HPOUTP -> C38 -> T1 -> R13 470R -> TX_INJ); C38 blocks\n  HPOUTP's ~0.85 V common mode; D2 BAT54S clamps HPOUTP; single-ended\n  HPOUTP is not a documented mode (UG-2257); firmware sets HP_MODE = 1\n  (line out). T1 is not a flight part (-20 C min, UL60950).\n\nRX - EARPHONE AUDIO TO THE CUPS, T2/T3 (Triad SP-74, one per cup)\n- Primaries in parallel across RX_RING / AC_GND. Secondaries in parallel\n  (3+5 / 4+6) to J6 (left cup) and J7 (right cup) as XF_SEC_A/B_L and _R.\n  Each cup board receives the pair on its J5 (XF_SEC_A/XF_SEC_B).\n- One SP-74 per cup, not one shared: a shorted cable to one cup cannot\n  silence the other, and each part sees the per-cup load (32 ohm speaker\n  -> ~316 ohm; both cups ~158 ohm at the panel, inside its 150 ohm min).\n- Fail-passive switching is in each cup (U4/U5 AQW612S): unpowered, the\n  cup's speaker sits on this secondary. Powered, the cup switches to its\n  own HPOUT and panel audio is mixed or muted in DSP from its ADC2 tap.\n- The SP-74 isolates the cups and their speakers from aircraft ground.\n- GPIO_RLY_RX_MUTE_3V3 removed with K2; J1 pin 8 is now spare (no-connect).\n\nOPEN\n1. RLY_COIL_SUPPLY keeps its name, but it now feeds U12's LEDs, not a coil.\n2. AQW612S: no THD spec; \"not for automotive use\" per its datasheet.\n3. SP-74: 300 Hz lower corner; core level at full panel volume needs a\n   bench measurement (see kicad/cup-board/README.md).\n4. J4/J5/J6/J7 are generic placeholders, as before."
    (at 470 190 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid "046b613a-2acc-4f7e-ac37-168751ca48f8")
  )
